<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">

    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>incident-management-platform</artifactId>
    <version>1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <packaging>pom</packaging>

    <name>Incident Management Platform</name>
    <description>Microservices-based incident management platform</description>
<!-- Goal: The whole point of putting modules in a parent pom.xml is such that
 1.we  define properties like Java version, Spring Boot etc here in root pom file
and  every module automatically inherit it — instead of repeating the same setting in 11 different files.
  2. we use it to build entire project with one command. instead of building each service seperately.

why is it not working right now?
here the second point is only working, first pont is not working because:
right now our parent pom file is passing down the settings(properties) to its children (modules).
But this will only works if a child modules actually says: "this is my parent." But right none of our  11 modules say "the root pom.xml is my parent."
Instead, every single one of them says:"My parent is spring-boot-starter-parent" (a Spring Boot file, not your root file).
why we are not fixing it?
why we are no solving this now?
because then spring boot each service verion management is handled by the this root file.
but we have Two modules where:
1.common-security is intentionally using an older Spring Boot version (3.3.2) instead of the newer one everyone else uses (3.5.11)
2.Ai-Service is intentionally using Java 17 instead of Java 21
 So it is not mechanical - it forces decisions about two intentional
         exceptions. That is its own task, not a side effect of fixing the build.
         Both exceptions are recorded in BUGS-TO-FIX-LATER.md (E5, E6).
  -->
    <modules>
        <!-- Shared libraries: plain JARs, not runnable. Everything else depends on these. -->
        <module>shared-events</module>      <!-- Kafka event classes -->
        <module>common-security</module>    <!-- HeaderAuthFilter -->
        <module>common-web</module>         <!-- error handling: exceptions + handler + traceId -->
        <module>common-kafka</module>       <!-- Kafka safety net: retry + dead letter topic -->

        <!-- Infrastructure services -->
        <module>Eureka</module>             <!-- service registry -->
        <module>APIGateway</module>         <!-- JWT check + header injection -->

        <!-- Business services -->
        <module>AuthService</module>
        <module>UserService</module>
        <module>IncidentService</module>
        <module>NotificationService</module>
        <module>ReportingService</module>
        <module>Ai-Service</module>
    </modules>

    <properties>
        <java.version>21</java.version>
        <maven.compiler.source>21</maven.compiler.source>
        <maven.compiler.target>21</maven.compiler.target>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <spring-boot.version>3.5.11</spring-boot.version>
        <spring-cloud.version>2025.0.1</spring-cloud.version>
    </properties>

</project>

